QA round 6 — reasoning for future loops.

Why IPAddressDeny=any and not something smaller: systemd has no ingress-only
knob. RestrictNetworkInterfaces=lo and PrivateNetwork=yes both also kill
egress, and PrivateNetwork additionally hides the app from Caddy. Blocking
peer addresses is the only lever that leaves Caddy->app working. Consequence
is total: the app cannot call anybody. If a future loop wants outbound calls,
add per-unit IPAddressAllow= CIDRs; do not go back to 'any'.

Why deps move to apply time rather than a venv: uv sync --script + a
UV_CACHE_DIR the unit owns is ~15 lines through the System seam. Building a
venv under /opt would have needed stale_payload exclusions, a new artifact
row in the Scope table, and its own ownership rules. Verified by hand and by
tests/test_e2e.py::test_a_pep723_app_starts_offline_from_the_cache_apply_built,
which resolves a real package and then starts with --offline, so it fails if
apply ever stops populating the cache.

Why a group and not an ACL for static payloads: setfacl does not exist on
macOS, so an ACL-based fix could never be exercised by this repo's tests, and
it needs the acl package plus a mount option on the host. A supplementary
group needs neither. The wrinkle is that supplementary groups are read at
process start, so the group action restarts Caddy instead of reloading it.
That restart only ever happens on the first apply of a static unit.

Why created-dirs instead of a fixed PRUNE_DIRS list: the old list walked
parents, so an empty /opt or /etc/systemd/system could be removed even though
smallapp never made it. Recording the topmost directory each mkdir had to
create is the only version that can honestly claim 'only what we created'.
The record is per-process plus a persisted file, because rm runs in a
different process from apply.

Why resolve_secrets now takes 'known': the env file is not evidence that the
apply finished. Only the registry's complete flag is. Rotating on an
incomplete unit is safe (nobody has a session yet); reusing is not (nobody
ever saw the token).

Still unverified on this machine: every chgrp/chown/group-membership path is
